{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"direct-category","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Direct categories"}]},"title_text":"Direct categories","kind":"definition","taxon":null,"url":"direct-category.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","direct-category"],["kind","definition"],["label","Definition"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"A "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"well-founded order"}]},{"Text":" is a set "},{"Math":{"src":"D"}},{"Text":" with a proposition-valued transitive relation "},{"Math":{"src":"<"}},{"Text":" admitting no infinite descent: every element is accessible. Write "},{"Math":{"src":"a ≤ b"}},{"Text":" for "},{"Math":{"src":"lr(( a < b )) ∨ lr(( a = b ))"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"A "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"direct structure"}]},{"Text":" on a category "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(C)"}},{"Text":" over "},{"Math":{"src":"lr(( D \\, < ))"}},{"Text":" is a functor"}]},{"Math":{"src":"\"deg\" : cal(C) -> lr(( D \\, ≤ ))"}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"into the well-founded order viewed as a poset category. The functor organizes two pieces of data at once: an ordering on the objects, and the invariant that morphisms respect it — "},{"Math":{"src":"f : x -> y"}},{"Text":" forces "},{"Math":{"src":"\"deg\" x ≤ \"deg\" y"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"A direct structure equips the objects with a well-founded strict relation"}]},{"Math":{"src":"x ≺ y ⟺ \"deg\" x < \"deg\" y ."}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Intuitively, direct categories are the right generalization of well-foundedness to the categorical setting: a direct category is essentially one whose underlying graph is a directed acyclic graph, layered by degree, so that data at an object may be defined by recursion from data at all objects strictly below it."}]},{"Group":{"role":"ext-svg","attrs":[["svg","<svg class=\"helia-typst-svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 196.762244095 123.742913386\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"19.676em\" height=\"12.374em\"